[{:db/id 17592186316816 :answer-field/correct 17592186316277 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186435710 :answer-field/correct "answer-065c1236-c8cd-5e0a-8536-ab48d1fe6aae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-065c1236-c8cd-5e0a-8536-ab48d1fe6aae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-065c1236-c8cd-5e0a-8536-ab48d1fe6aae" :answer/id #uuid "065c1236-c8cd-5e0a-8536-ab48d1fe6aae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231429 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ee642054-1d27-50a4-8f05-345ca578dfc0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ee642054-1d27-50a4-8f05-345ca578dfc0" :question/id #uuid "ee642054-1d27-50a4-8f05-345ca578dfc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-343743" :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The particle is acted on by an external periodic force\n$f(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$\nAssuming the system experiences resonance, which of the following could be used to represent the general solution for the position $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)-\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$\n\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants." :question/worked-solution "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $3.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =3.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =3$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[9(D-Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-9(C+Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)]+9t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ 9D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-9C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and $D=0.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)-\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)-\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$\n\nOnly solution II matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c3260424-876c-50ae-ac8b-7b96731c9907"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3260424-876c-50ae-ac8b-7b96731c9907" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3260424-876c-50ae-ac8b-7b96731c9907" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8b3b3ddc-f2b0-5960-a120-6e3182615388" :answer-field/choices ["answer-720de89b-25be-516b-9df5-32bca90894e6" "answer-eb5401b3-3249-566f-8e5f-01020ae0590b" "answer-10ac45f2-8682-5e38-90a5-af6b3b0df052" "answer-8b3b3ddc-f2b0-5960-a120-6e3182615388" "answer-90774d44-8df7-5a01-b829-eff4553b5ba9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-720de89b-25be-516b-9df5-32bca90894e6" :answer/id #uuid "720de89b-25be-516b-9df5-32bca90894e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb5401b3-3249-566f-8e5f-01020ae0590b" :answer/id #uuid "eb5401b3-3249-566f-8e5f-01020ae0590b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10ac45f2-8682-5e38-90a5-af6b3b0df052" :answer/id #uuid "10ac45f2-8682-5e38-90a5-af6b3b0df052" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b3b3ddc-f2b0-5960-a120-6e3182615388" :answer/id #uuid "8b3b3ddc-f2b0-5960-a120-6e3182615388" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90774d44-8df7-5a01-b829-eff4553b5ba9" :answer/id #uuid "90774d44-8df7-5a01-b829-eff4553b5ba9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317431 :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The particle is acted on by an external periodic force\n$f(t)=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$\nAssuming the system experiences resonance, which of the following could be used to represent the general solution for the position $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants." :question/worked-solution "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $3.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =3.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =3$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[(6D-9Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-(6C+9Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)]+9t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ 6D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-6C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $D=-2.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nSolutions I, II, and III match the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d9d2f46d-5baa-5bef-85ef-5cb27486297b" :activity/id #uuid "d9d2f46d-5baa-5bef-85ef-5cb27486297b" :activity/title "Resonance in Vibrating Systems" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048966 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-5ee37f4e-428d-5c80-b898-6258e65e6514" "step-83ab17b5-350b-529d-97cb-ee01d416ef71" "step-c4c6cf6d-8b3b-5c57-b551-475a3ee53347" "step-102631d9-03a3-5a77-8b43-d3ebf3037f1b" "step-63616043-21be-5d80-99e6-bbe839235312"] :activity/first-step "step-5ee37f4e-428d-5c80-b898-6258e65e6514" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5ee37f4e-428d-5c80-b898-6258e65e6514" :step/id #uuid "5ee37f4e-428d-5c80-b898-6258e65e6514" :step/content 17592186317422 :step/next "step-83ab17b5-350b-529d-97cb-ee01d416ef71" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-83ab17b5-350b-529d-97cb-ee01d416ef71" :step/id #uuid "83ab17b5-350b-529d-97cb-ee01d416ef71" :step/content 17592186435716 :step/next "step-c4c6cf6d-8b3b-5c57-b551-475a3ee53347" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c4c6cf6d-8b3b-5c57-b551-475a3ee53347" :step/id #uuid "c4c6cf6d-8b3b-5c57-b551-475a3ee53347" :step/content "question-ee642054-1d27-50a4-8f05-345ca578dfc0" :step/next "step-102631d9-03a3-5a77-8b43-d3ebf3037f1b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-102631d9-03a3-5a77-8b43-d3ebf3037f1b" :step/id #uuid "102631d9-03a3-5a77-8b43-d3ebf3037f1b" :step/content 17592186435720 :step/next "step-63616043-21be-5d80-99e6-bbe839235312" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-63616043-21be-5d80-99e6-bbe839235312" :step/id #uuid "63616043-21be-5d80-99e6-bbe839235312" :step/content 17592186317431 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
